    "turn_idx": 0,
    "turn_text": "This is AgriPulse Open Mike. I'm your host, Jeff Daly. Our guest this week is U.S. Senate Agriculture Ranking Member, John Bozeman. AgriPulse Open Mike is brought to you by Bayer, helping meet the challenges of sustainability to help shape possibilities and our vision of health for all, hunger for none. AgriPulse Open Mike continues with Arkansas U.S. Senator, John Bozeman. Next, As a leader in the industry, we at Bayer have the opportunity and responsibility to help address the challenges around sustainability and ensure that we can all thrive while using our planet's resources in a sustainable way. Sustainability is an integral part of our operations, and we believe that farmers and agriculture can be part of the solution to many of the planet's biggest challenges. Whether that's helping growers utilize new technologies to get more out of their land, or incentivizing carbon smart practices such as strip or no-till and planting cover crops, we are committed to innovate, grow and partner with farmers to help shape what's possible and further our vision of health for all, hunger for none. For more on Bayer Sustainability Efforts, visit Bayer.com forward slash EN forward slash sustainability. This is Agropulse Open Mike. A litany of issues including the COVID pandemic, adverse weather, labor shortages and supply chain disruptions have shifted obstacles in the agriculture paradigm. U.S. Senate AG ranking member John Bozeman says the Russian Ukraine conflict has tilted the balance not only of global food production but world hunger.",
