    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72683.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Nobody really expected the Ukraine government the Ukraine people to stand up the way they did are vaunted CIA and intelligence and these are good folks that work hard and they are generally right but they got this very wrong they told us that They would be in the Russians would be in the Kaplan four or five days that hasn't been the case. This is drug on for an extended period of time, which is great. We're trying to give them the resources so they can not only hold their own, but they can win the war. And that's that's actually doing fairly well. But what's happened is result of that right now that the Ukrainians, the Russians should be in the field planning. They're not doing that. They're both fighting a war. So the resources, the diesel, the machinery even is being taken to other places. So they're not planning. And so it has changed the world in a sense, 18% of the corn, 30% of the wheat, a good portion of the safflower oil, all of these things that are so, so very important. Not just for that region. These are worldwide numbers. It really is remarkable. They truly are the breadbasket of that part of the world. So it's changed. We need to account for it. We're really trying to figure out what it's going to do to commodity prices in the future. what it's going to do. Also, the prospect of actually food shortages.",
