    "turn_text": "No, I think very definitely. Half of the food stuff of Africa comes from this region of the country. So rather than being reactive as things fall apart, I'd like for us to be now putting in the policies to keep that from happening. We don't do a very good job of that. And as to what that is, I'm really not sure. But I think we need to think outside the box. Because you've got a situation, not only are we concerned about shortages, but with very, very high commodity prices. People like the World Food Bank. They've got a finite amount of money, and as commodity prices go up, it's not magic. The money doesn't go as far. They can't buy as much. And so that's where Secretary Beasley, David Beasley, made the statement about the hungry to the starving. And that's only exacerbating.",
