    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72683.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "Well, there's a number of different things that we're working on. Dusty Johnson has a good bill. We have a bill in the Senate trying to make it such that we can free our ports up to make them more efficient. So we're working that angle. We are trying to figure out the supply chain. A lot of that is labor-based and it doesn't matter what industry you're in. So we've got to make it such that we're more efficient with the supply chain. On time delivery is so efficient prior to the pandemic. I think we need to rethink all of that. not only on time but right then delivery. We don't have warehouses like we used to to anticipate some of these things. So I think there's a number of things that we can do and everybody is working good faith, I think, to figure those out.",
