    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72683.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 18,
    "turn_text": "Well, I really enjoyed being with Chairwoman Stabenow at Michigan State. That is an institution that has done a tremendous job through the years. The place that we actually had at uses a lot of laminated wood construction, and it's an old thing that is re-surging. I think it shows great opportunity for our foresters, and great opportunity for climate. It's a question a lot of carbon. But we heard from probably 15, 16 witnesses, lots of witnesses, and really hearing about Kind of what's going on in their lives right now, and there is a lot of uncertainty They're concerned about the future We heard some about the regulatory atmosphere and the list goes on and on so the good news is I was there center stab and I was there most of my staff was there Most of her staff was there also and they were busy you know scribbling notes, so I think we got some good takeaways and you know as we go forward that's really what we hope to do in Arkansas is just let producers talk and the you know the South Southern agriculture is different than Michigan and although Michigan is blessed they've got a lot of water they can grow you know basically anything but we'll be talking to our producers about you know the problems they're having and then you know working together",
