  {
    "episode_id": 72683,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/2/72683.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "No, I think it comes before the farm bill and my concern there is making sure that what we do actually makes a difference. The problem is we have a very high price at the retail level as you go and buy a steak, whatever. And then again, our producers, the people who work so hard, particularly at the cow cafe, are not able to participate as much in that price. So, what do you do about it? And Grassy Fisher has a solution, or what they feel like is a solution. My problem is, as I talk to The economists talk to people, you know, Randy Blockett, cattle facts, people like that. There's just no consensus at all if that's going to make any difference. And so you go down the pathway of heavily regulating things and yet really not making a difference. In fact, most of the economists feel like not only would it be neutral, but in some cases it would actually cost producers money, okay? So that's really where we're at. We had a really good hearing. We're going to have more discussion. We're in the process now of getting USDA's thoughts on that from their economist. But the two things I think that we do agree on totally is an industry. I used to have a bunch of cows as an industry is we need increased competition at the slaughter level. We also need more transparency. And one thing that I would argue in talking to our economist on the committee is USDA now is putting out a tremendous amount of information. The problem is nobody understands it. Our economists can understand it after really literally sitting down working through it for several hours. We need a one pager that makes it such that the average person involved in the industry can extrapolate that good data from that so it can help them make decisions going forward. So those two things I think we agree on. There's wide disagreement within the industry. So I have to work through that.",
